<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:42:34Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Trump puts new Russia sanctions on hold</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b76fa5c8b51955bcc2b6fad54074322c0f6ebd87e7b11ee5dd03a91871d0e87d</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:42:29Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T02:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-puts-new-russia-sanctions-on-hold/a-79685002--586e2562981b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-puts-new-russia-sanctions-on-hold/a-79685002?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US president cited national interests for his decision to sign a waiver on sanctions Congress voted to place on Russia.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil: Amazon deforestation lowest in nearly 40 years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ed73a1a16200ec2c642a86c8396f1d589b66edfd646da89f5ba81267e9557465</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:42:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T22:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/brazil-amazon-deforestation-lowest-in-nearly-40-years/a-79684906--24b7e4d329ee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/brazil-amazon-deforestation-lowest-in-nearly-40-years/a-79684906?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The latest figures show that 3,335 square kilometers of the Amazon rainforest were cleared in the year ending in July, the lowest level since 1988. The drop has been described as an "historic achievement."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ukrainian President Zelenskyy speaks at EU summit amid spat with Donald Trump</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:284763a133c1d543cb26c45f8ae5ca94c3352fa931c3ca0e42982c4d6921fada</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:42:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T19:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukrainian-president-zelenskyy-speaks-at-eu-summit-amid-spat-with-donald-trump/a-79684340--6307cb90b3ba.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukrainian-president-zelenskyy-speaks-at-eu-summit-amid-spat-with-donald-trump/a-79684340?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">EU leaders reaffirmed support for Ukraine at the Brussels summit. But souring relations with the US over Russia and Starlink and a big hole in the budget will make for a difficult winter for Ukraine.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>West Bank: US journalist injured by Israeli settlers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1d0a4f18f18d3860db9082beac93631663b9292d112fd5ba790403d923a6edb4</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T19:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/west-bank-us-journalist-injured-by-israeli-settlers/a-79684181--8e9b6bd6853f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/west-bank-us-journalist-injured-by-israeli-settlers/a-79684181?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Washington Post journalist Heidi Levine said she was beaten by Israeli settlers in the occupied West Bank. Reporters Without Borders slammed the attack as "brazen violence."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>White House press secretary Zacharia exiting role after short tenure</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d6b5ca4b0140518e82b53a03d61f5593e8a510e17b9089769eb724e64b6839eb</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T19:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/white-house-press-secretary-zacharia-exiting-role-after-short-tenure/a-79684341--2f88277a7fd8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/white-house-press-secretary-zacharia-exiting-role-after-short-tenure/a-79684341?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Zacharia, having served only five days in the role, is now the shortest-serving press secretary in White House history. Her departure follows a rocky debut at the podium and controversy surrounding her background.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Hijab ban at schools in Azerbaijan: What's behind the rare wave of protests?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e468adee355c31b7882d1c4d84e4018960687f578027d2e2b6f385c4d4aea958</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T17:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hijab-ban-at-schools-in-azerbaijan-what-s-behind-the-rare-wave-of-protests/a-79683716--35e52a17baf3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hijab-ban-at-schools-in-azerbaijan-what-s-behind-the-rare-wave-of-protests/a-79683716?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Girls wearing headscarves have been turned away from schools in Azerbaijan, triggering unusual protests involving children. The government rules do not mention hijabs. Why are schools enforcing unwritten rules?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>At summit, EU leaders pledge support for Ukraine's Zelenskyy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:52498e1ae42616b1f3bf6168937775742deb9e6c8a0bae0c84f177e1e8f865e6</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T17:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/at-summit-eu-leaders-pledge-support-for-ukraine-s-zelenskyy/a-79678808--25caad1f3ce4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/at-summit-eu-leaders-pledge-support-for-ukraine-s-zelenskyy/a-79678808?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">President Zelenskyy has received words of encouragement from EU leaders, who pledged support for Ukraine's self-defense against Russia. This comes as winter approaches and the US seems to be withdrawing support.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia's Abiy Ahmed appoints interim Tigray government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3739db6d126ee2a27414ddac968ad3ab2f5fead10ab3d236ff53ef2f2cfb6a69</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T16:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ethiopia-s-abiy-ahmed-appoints-interim-tigray-government/a-79683519--c9a39db6c855.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ethiopia-s-abiy-ahmed-appoints-interim-tigray-government/a-79683519?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Abiy Ahmed's office said there would be elections held in Tigray within 6 months. The move comes after an escalation in fighting between federal forces and a rebel alliance.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany, France agree on deal to support Europe's struggling car industry</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:57decffb753f58dde4e20026b9c2ed976d923b61d5a0e9999de388a61a2c63c0</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T15:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-france-agree-on-deal-to-support-europe-s-struggling-car-industry/a-79678595--5e23597ac466.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-france-agree-on-deal-to-support-europe-s-struggling-car-industry/a-79678595?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The two countries said the agreement aimed to safeguard Europe's automotive industry, encouraging development and research. Automakers in Europe have so far struggled to compete with Chinese electric car companies.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo recovering from surgery, will deliver Sunday prayer</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ed7c338dd91a5bc6a514e2cd9f61ad9d2de1819dcd6f944bd35bfc41077f8c23</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T15:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pope-leo-recovering-from-surgery-will-deliver-sunday-prayer/a-79682540--e275bd782fd4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pope-leo-recovering-from-surgery-will-deliver-sunday-prayer/a-79682540?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Vatican has said that Pope Leo XIV is recovering from lung surgery. Photos released on Friday showed the pontiff celebrating Mass at Rome's Gemelli Hospital unaided.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>German colonialism on agenda in Bundestag debate on Namibia genocide</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a0d9fdc10b2adc77a3e07e7f855d6e7c11aa7ab7f5ae7944b1bdad3b26a634cf</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T14:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-colonialism-on-agenda-in-bundestag-debate-on-namibia-genocide/a-79682388--e473209aeb4e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-colonialism-on-agenda-in-bundestag-debate-on-namibia-genocide/a-79682388?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Opposition parties have forced a debate in the Bundestag on the early-20th-century genocide Germany carried out in Namibia. Will this finally spur progress in addressing colonial crimes?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Iran: When 'honor' becomes a death sentence for women</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:46a3c51a978bf1886dbc7cb4b4e0a7c755ae9e3092a088a7ef8426b2836cfd6f</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T14:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-when-honor-becomes-a-death-sentence-for-women/a-79681977--275bc2dc6f2d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-when-honor-becomes-a-death-sentence-for-women/a-79681977?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The murder of a young mother has once again sparked debate in Iran over so-called honor killings, the social acceptance of violence against women and the lack of protection for people vulnerable to misogynist violence.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Albania: Students demand political change and resignation of Prime Minister Edi Rama</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:020a01517e0d5a8bffa4c6af14dcc2e51dd343c29370026e74b39ade2e749b28</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T14:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/albania-students-demand-political-change-and-resignation-of-prime-minister-edi-rama/a-79682217--699ae649993b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/albania-students-demand-political-change-and-resignation-of-prime-minister-edi-rama/a-79682217?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Empty lecture halls, burning buildings and demands for change: Albanian students are spearheading a protest movement that has become the biggest challenge to Prime Minister Edi Rama in years.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Houthi attacks on strategic Saudi assets threaten Riyadh's regional leadership and economic ambitions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:08a278fa62d31ccd527824033fc450fcdd214a06d548050c2d888a7758a6dad5</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T14:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/houthi-attacks-on-strategic-saudi-assets-threaten-riyadh-s-regional-leadership-and-economic-ambition/a-79680200--af5776370a6d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/houthi-attacks-on-strategic-saudi-assets-threaten-riyadh-s-regional-leadership-and-economic-ambitions/a-79680200?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Yemen's Iran-backed Houthis continue to target Saudi Arabia, Riyadh's vulnerability threatens its claim on regional and religious leadership — as well as its standing as an economic powerhouse.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>The EU wants an AI revolution. But on whose terms?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6ab36f5f3b345bd8d299797fce4baff89c3b218e5bd3c48de7d00558c69e134a</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T13:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-eu-wants-an-ai-revolution-but-on-whose-terms/a-79673456--ab198d15d72f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-eu-wants-an-ai-revolution-but-on-whose-terms/a-79673456?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As the US and China race ahead, the European Union seeks to boost its economy with AI. Can it compete while protecting workers, safety and the climate?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India's young workers have a new colleague: AI</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:54edfe9292b8958f08e295bf9dd5d91d48a18ea00d7f193119996d6580101ea1</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T11:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-s-young-workers-have-a-new-colleague-ai/a-79678342--60612fda0623.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-s-young-workers-have-a-new-colleague-ai/a-79678342?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Artificial intelligence is changing the way Indian workplaces operate — raising questions about productivity, skills and entry-level jobs.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>German lawmakers back monthly state pension contributions for children, with families able to add more.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3d10672efa2e52bc5d9fb6cef0126f3540bd9dd0e9cb718aece8eaf691f60b0c</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T11:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-lawmakers-back-monthly-state-pension-contributions-for-children-with-families-able-to-add-mor/live-79678671--02713419dab3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-lawmakers-back-monthly-state-pension-contributions-for-children-with-families-able-to-add-more/live-79678671?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's parliament has backed a plan to help children save for retirement from the age of 6. Meanwhile, Jewish students report death threats after they confronted a far-right lawmaker.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>How prepared is Kenya for an Ebola outbreak?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e2a186c8dca7cd6037bbaf423d88ac0003bdb57ef2e35cede02006f19fc7a65a</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T10:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-prepared-is-kenya-for-an-ebola-outbreak/a-79668144--2b6e19c28555.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-prepared-is-kenya-for-an-ebola-outbreak/a-79668144?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The first two confirmed Ebola cases in Kenya have raised urgent questions about the country's public health preparedness and border controls. But the Health Ministry says there is no need for panic.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Italy cuts air traffic in half amid data transmission issue</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:178e2288dd58f0811484d94c29cc620ec19a0d469659f658142fbb8d529c5387</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T10:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/italy-cuts-air-traffic-in-half-amid-data-transmission-issue/a-79678133--8d0677d89358.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/italy-cuts-air-traffic-in-half-amid-data-transmission-issue/a-79678133?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Citing problems with the data transmission network, Italian authorities have drastically reduced the volume of flights in their airspace. The ENAV authority ruled out malicious activity and said flights remained safe.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Clashes erupt at Argentine student protests against President Milei's austerity policies</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:82bda858bc1b1598ee11b6599684f7579d96e5ec22c5341ef6fb3751d7361cb5</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T09:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/clashes-erupt-at-argentine-student-protests-against-president-milei-s-austerity-policies/a-79676861--35bb07407c1a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/clashes-erupt-at-argentine-student-protests-against-president-milei-s-austerity-policies/a-79676861?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Demonstrators clashed with police as President Javier Milei's decision not to release funding for universities brought students and employees to the streets. Protesters say the country's future is at stake.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Who was Eva Mamlok? Berlin square renamed after Jewish anti-fascist resistance fighter</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9d893f36a3a35e474b1000f1a6ebd7908cce23af7245fd63f3c12882b11978d1</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T09:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/who-was-eva-mamlok-berlin-square-renamed-after-jewish-anti-fascist-resistance-fighter/a-79668919--fa371a8e7f27.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/who-was-eva-mamlok-berlin-square-renamed-after-jewish-anti-fascist-resistance-fighter/a-79668919?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">She started taking action against Hitler as a teenager and never stopped until her death in a concentration camp. Berlin's Blücherplatz is now being renamed after her.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry></feed>
